G5 — END-TO-END MANUAL REPLAY                          DEFERRED-MANUAL-QA
=============================

Scenarios A through E require a running stack (api + worker + mosquitto +
postgres + a Web Push subscription on a real Android device). None of
these are available in this gate environment. Per the prompt's own
acceptance text on slice 0010 (criterion #5 / #6) and the gate's
"Honesty check" (G9), each scenario is marked DEFERRED-MANUAL-QA with
the supporting code-level evidence listed below.

Scenario A — locked-vehicle latch survives restart
  Code evidence:
    - alert_rule_state.last_fired_at + last_fired_severity persisted
      across restart (slice 0002 / migration 000193).
    - Engine rehydrates state on first observation per (rule, vehicle)
      via SnapshotPoolBatch / GetState pattern (rule_engine.go).
    - Tests: `TestEngineRehydratesLatchFromState`,
      `TestLatchClearedOnFallingEdge` (rule_engine_test.go).

Scenario B — unlocked-vehicle escalation
  Code evidence:
    - escalation_after_min + escalation_severity stamped at first-fire
      via ConditionStartedAt (in-memory) + LastFiredAt (DB) (slice 0009).
    - Engine promotes severity once duration elapsed (rule_engine.go
      ~L420 `if elapsed >= escalationAfter`).
    - Tests: `TestEvaluate_Escalation_NotYetTriggered`,
      `TestEvaluate_Escalation_TriggeredAfterDuration`,
      `TestEvaluate_Escalation_OnceModeIgnored`,
      `TestEvaluate_Escalation_NilFieldsBaseSeverity`.

Scenario C — multi-select sticky-all
  Code evidence:
    - all_vehicles=true causes engine to evaluate against every active
      vehicle in the snapshot map (slice 0005).
    - Tests: `TestSnapshotPoolBatch_StickyAll`,
      `TestSnapshotPoolBatch_NewVehicleAfterRuleCreate`.

Scenario D — force-choose smart defaults
  Code evidence:
    - canSave gate requires triggerMode ∈ {'once','repeat'}, never
      defaults silently (slice 0008 + 0009 both extend canSave).
    - Tests: `TestAlertStudioPage_RecommendationBannerWithoutForcing`,
      `TestAlertStudioPage_SaveDisabledUntilTriggerModeChosen`.

Scenario E — notification icon de-duplication (slice 0010)
  Code evidence (this slice's three-layer safety net):
    - Backend `Payload.Icon` field DELETED (struct walk +
      JSON-marshal regression tests in service_test.go).
    - Frontend `PushPayload.icon?` REMOVED + `options.icon` never
      assigned in showNotification (sw.ts + sw.test.ts contract).
    - Acceptance #5 (real Android visual) and #6 (DevTools sim)
      DEFERRED — see phase-49-0010 log for rationale. The 3-layer pin
      is judged sufficient to prevent silent regression.


G6 — METRICS SURFACE                                              YELLOW
====================

The prompt's verification regex was:

  grep -E '^tesla_alert_rules_(snooze_skipped|cooldown_skipped|
                               max_fires_cap_hit|escalated)_total'

This regex would NOT match any actually-exposed metric — the existing
counters use the prefix `teslasync_cep_rules_*` (legacy convention from
phases pre-49) and the new escalation counter from slice 0009 uses
`teslasync_alert_rules_escalated_total`. The intent of the check
(verify the four counters exist) IS satisfied:

  internal/metrics/metrics.go:126  AlertRulesCooldownSkipped
                                   → teslasync_cep_rules_cooldown_skipped_total
  internal/metrics/metrics.go:132  AlertRulesSnoozeSkipped
                                   → teslasync_cep_rules_snooze_skipped_total
  internal/metrics/metrics.go:142  AlertRulesMaxFiresCapHit
                                   → teslasync_cep_rules_max_fires_cap_hit_total
  internal/metrics/metrics.go:154  AlertRulesHourlyCapHit (added slice 0004)
                                   → teslasync_cep_rules_hourly_cap_hit_total
  internal/metrics/metrics.go:166  AlertRulesEscalated
                                   → teslasync_alert_rules_escalated_total

All five counters are registered, exported, and incremented at the
correct gate sites (verified by their respective unit tests). The
prefix INCONSISTENCY between `cep_rules_` (legacy) and `alert_rules_`
(slice 0009) is a HOUSEKEEPING follow-up: rename
`alert_rules_escalated_total` to `cep_rules_escalated_total` for
consistency with the surrounding counters in the next phase, OR
rename the four `cep_rules_*` to `alert_rules_*` if the
domain-canonical name is preferred. Either rename is a one-character
change to the metric Name field; neither blocks Phase-49.

The actual Prometheus endpoint scrape (`curl …/metrics`) is SKIPPED
for the same reason as G3/G4 — no running API instance in this gate
environment.


